# MCP Configuration (optional)

If the main agent supports MCP over SSE, use this configuration instead of REST:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "agent-mesh": {
      "type": "sse",
      "baseUrl": "http://<orchestrator-host>:8001",
      "customHeaders": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer <USER_TOKEN>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> `USER_TOKEN` is a user token (the short-lived session token returned by `POST /api/auth/login`, or the long-lived API token returned once when the user is created / rotated via `POST /api/auth/users/{username}/token`). The global `AGENT_MESH_TOKEN` is **not** accepted on the MCP channel.

Available MCP tools:

- `list_agents` — list all registered nodes
- `get_agent` — get a single node
- `get_agent_detail` — node profile + recent tasks
- `set_agent_alias` — set/clear node alias
- `dispatch_task` — dispatch a task (`agent_id`, `instruction`, `mode`)
- `get_task_status` — query task status
- `list_tasks` — list tasks
- `poll_for_task` — edge heartbeat (internal)
- `submit_result` — edge result submission (internal)

Notes:

- `agent_id` accepts a numeric id, a loopback MAC (e.g. `00:11:22:33:44:55`), or a display name.
- `mode` is required for `dispatch_task`: `command` (shell verbatim) or `llm` (opencode).
- The SSE endpoint lives on port **8001**; REST/Web is on **8000**.

This is provided as a convenience reference; see `skills/agent-mesh/SKILL.md` for the full usage guide.
